<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>@app-id@</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>
  <name>Septima</name>
  <summary>Browse and create modern-codec 7-Zip archives</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      Septima is a GTK frontend for 7-Zip ZS (7zz) that speaks modern
      compression codecs — Zstandard, Brotli and Fast-LZMA2 — with a real
      compression-tuning interface. It is an archive tool, not a file manager.
    </p>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">@app-id@.desktop</launchable>
  <screenshots>
    <screenshot type="default">
      <caption>Choosing a modern codec in the Add-to-Archive dialog</caption>
      <image>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/superuser-miguel/septima/main/docs/screenshots/codec-menu.png</image>
    </screenshot>
    <screenshot>
      <caption>Reactive tuning with a live memory estimate</caption>
      <image>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/superuser-miguel/septima/main/docs/screenshots/create-dialog.png</image>
    </screenshot>
    <screenshot>
      <caption>Executable optimization, split volumes and encryption</caption>
      <image>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/superuser-miguel/septima/main/docs/screenshots/create-options.png</image>
    </screenshot>
    <screenshot>
      <caption>Opening an archive</caption>
      <image>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/superuser-miguel/septima/main/docs/screenshots/welcome.png</image>
    </screenshot>
  </screenshots>
  <url type="homepage">https://github.com/superuser-miguel/septima</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/superuser-miguel/septima/issues</url>
  <developer id="io.github.superuser_miguel">
    <name>Miguel Almanzar</name>
  </developer>
  <content_rating type="oars-1.1"/>
  <releases>
    <release version="0.5.0" date="2026-08-16">
      <description>
        <p>Batch encryption with a portable passwords file, and drag-out extraction.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Batch encrypt — when you create a separate archive for each item, Septima can give every archive its own random 64-character password and record them in a passwords file you keep wherever you keep secrets.</li>
          <li>The passwords file is plain, readable JSON, or protected with a password of its own (standard OpenPGP, so any gpg can open it). You choose before the run starts, so a protected run never writes plaintext to disk.</li>
          <li>Open a passwords file in Septima later — with the Open button, by dropping it in, or from the command line — and it offers to extract every archive it lists, each with its recorded password, into its own folder. Pick all of them or just the ones you want.</li>
          <li>Every password is written to disk before the first archive is created, and the file is rewritten after each one completes, so an interrupted run never leaves an archive whose password was lost.</li>
          <li>Drag entries out of an open archive into Files — or any app that accepts files — and they arrive extracted. Dragging a folder brings its whole subtree.</li>
          <li>Fixed: saved presets now remember the encryption method, the checksum-file switch, and the batch password choices, instead of quietly dropping them.</li>
          <li>Fixed: in batch mode, archive names come from the items themselves, so the archive-name field is greyed out rather than looking like it still applies.</li>
          <li>Fixed: batch archives are no longer written next to files opened through the file chooser, where they would land in a portal directory instead of a folder you can find.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.4.0" date="2026-08-10">
      <description>
        <p>Repairs Brotli archive creation, and completes 7-Zip CLI parity for what the bundled engine can write.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Fixed: Brotli archives created with 0.3.0 were corrupt. Every .br stream and .tar.br archive it wrote failed its own integrity test, because Septima always passed a thread count and the bundled engine silently switches Brotli stream formats when it sees one. Existing broken files cannot be repaired — recreate them with this release.</li>
          <li>Fixed: .tar.br, .tar.lz5 and .tar.liz archives (and their .tbr / .tlz5 / .tliz short forms) can now be browsed and extracted in one step, as the other compressed tarballs already could.</li>
          <li>Fixed: Brotli archives written by other multithreaded tools now open correctly instead of being rejected.</li>
          <li>Fixed: .7z archives made elsewhere holding raw Brotli could not be opened at all. They now open normally.</li>
          <li>Architecture / filter picker — a real control for the filter family: Delta, ARM64, ARM/ARMT, PPC, SPARC, RISC-V and BCJ2, alongside x86 BCJ.</li>
          <li>Lizard family and level picker — choose among the four method families (fastLZ4 / LIZv1, with or without Huffman) instead of one flat 10–49 slider.</li>
          <li>Standalone single-stream creation — write a raw .zst, .br, .lz4, .lz5, .xz, .gz or .bz2 stream, not only a tar plus a compressor.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.3.0" date="2026-07-26">
      <description>
        <p>A 7-Zip CLI-parity release, plus a real-world encryption fix.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Fixed: extracting a password-protected zip now prompts for the password instead of failing — and no longer leaves an empty file behind on a wrong password.</li>
          <li>Complete hash calculator — CRC-64, MD5, SHA-1/384, SHA3-512 and BLAKE2sp added, and xxHash split into XXH32/XXH64.</li>
          <li>Zip encryption method — choose strong AES-256 instead of the weak ZipCrypto default.</li>
          <li>More format × codec combinations — XZ and Deflate64 inside zip, and Brotli/LZ4/LZ5/Lizard tarballs.</li>
          <li>Batch compress — turn several files or folders into one archive each.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.2.0" date="2026-07-24">
      <description>
        <p>A batch-and-verify release, plus in-place archive editing.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Batch extract — select or drop several archives at once and each unpacks into its own new folder, with one shared password for encrypted sets.</li>
          <li>In-archive edit — delete or rename entries directly, and verify integrity with a one-click Test Archive.</li>
          <li>Post-extract actions — a "Show in Files" button and an optional delete-the-archive-afterwards toggle.</li>
          <li>Generate a checksum file — optionally write a .sha256 alongside a newly created archive.</li>
          <li>Automatic updates via the project's signed Flatpak repo.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="0.1.0" date="2026-07-11">
      <description>
        <p>First release.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Browse, extract (with progress, cancel and password support), and create archives.</li>
          <li>Modern codecs — Zstandard, Brotli, Fast-LZMA2, LZ4/LZ5 and Lizard, alongside LZMA2, PPMd and BZip2.</li>
          <li>A compression-tuning dialog with reactive level ranges, a live memory estimate, split volumes and named presets.</li>
          <li>Transparent modern tarballs — create, browse and extract .tar.zst / .tar.xz in one gesture.</li>
          <li>A checksum calculator (CRC, SHA-256/512, SHA3, BLAKE3, xxHash) with verify-against-a-checksum-file.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>
</component>
